Great game;

Before this game, I had finished many, but rarely played them again. With STALKER, , I played through it and many mods, which were still emerging at that time. The immersion was excellent, for the time - it can't compete with more recent games like DayZ (mod or standalone) for immersion. There was a general sense of horror, particularly in the underground installations, and freedom since the game is not linear (a big plus for me). I still think that this is one of the best games I've ever played, and I go back to it every once in a while. The mods list is enormous as well, though I don't know how many are still easily available. Oblivion Lost (two version), Stalker Rebalanced, AMK, Priboi Story, ABC Inferno; I played them all. The game envionment was so compelling that it spurred my interest in learning more about the region, about the Chernobyl incident, and the works that inspired it (e.g. Roadside Picnic, Tarkovsky's film
).
One of the best aspects of Steam distribution, for me, is that older games are updated for newer software/hardware platforms, making them easily accessible for a longer period of time. Highly highly recommended. The graphics will be a bit dated, but there are also some great graphic enhancement mods as well.

